 "modules": [
  {
   "id": 1,
   "plugin": "Core",
   "model": "Notes",
   "data": {
    "text": "CAMERA ANGLE\nPatch any CV (0 to 10 V) into a jack. 0 V is the item's From setting, 10 V its To.\n\nCV-CC 1: MIDI channel 1, CC 1 to 16\n   1 Shot size\n   2 Angle height\n   3 Lens length\n   4 Dutch / level\n   5 Point of view\n   6 Angles per scene\n   7 Angles grouped\n   8 When the angle changes\n   9 Angle matched to the line\n  10 Angle matched to the action\n  11 Depth of field\n  12 Focus pull\n  13 Motion blur\n  14 Frame shape\n  15 Where the subject sits\n  16 The camera lens\nCV-CC 2: MIDI channel 1, CC 17 to 32\n   1 suite: Coverage\n   2 suite: Oner\n   3 suite: Looking up at power\n   4 suite: Small from above\n   5 suite: Close and private\n   6 suite: World off balance\n   7 suite: Found-footage feel\n   8 suite: Cut on the words\n   9 suite: Cut on the move\n  10 suite: Focus pull reveal\n  11 suite: Widescreen epic\n  12 pair: When shot size becomes close, volume drops\n  13 pair: When dread builds, the frame tilts\n  14 pair: When the feeling peaks, the shot gets closer\n  15 pair: When the status flips, the camera angle flips\n  16 pair: When we see through someone's eyes, the picture starts to shake\nCV-CC 3: MIDI channel 1, CC 33 to 47\n   1 pair: When the point of view is lying, the voice-over and the picture disagree\n   2 pair: When a scene has more angles, the cutting speeds up\n   3 pair: When each angle is picked for a line, the cuts land on the lines\n   4 pair: When the angle plays against the line, the joke lands\n   5 pair: When each angle is picked for the action, the cuts land on the moves\n   6 pair: When the angle fights the action, the audience feels uneasy\n   7 pair: When motion blur is taken away, action feels jittery and frightening\n   8 pair: When the background goes soft, all eyes go to the face\n   9 pair: When the focus shifts on a line, the speaker's face goes sharp\n  10 pair: When a character sits dead center, the scene plays as deadpan comedy\n  11 pair: When the frame suddenly widens, the moment feels like a victory\n  12 pairs: The camera follows the feeling\n  13 pairs: Whose eyes are these?\n  14 pairs: Choosing the angle\n  15 pairs: Where the eye goes"
   },
