  {
   "id": 24,
   "plugin": "Core",
   "model": "Notes",
   "data": {
    "text": "MOVEMENT WITH LINES\nPatch any CV (0 to 10 V) into a jack. 0 V is the item's From setting, 10 V its To.\n\nCV-CC 1: MIDI channel 3, CC 65 to 80\n   1 Size of gesture\n   2 Stillness\n   3 Blink\n   4 Anticipation\n   5 Leads the move\n   6 Facial expression\n   7 Eye darts\n   8 Posture\n   9 Touch\n  10 Walk and talk\n  11 Business with a prop\n  12 Move on the line\n  13 The listener's body\n  14 Saying it with their back turned\n  15 A habit of their own\n  16 Copying each other's body\nCV-CC 2: MIDI channel 3, CC 81 to 96\n   1 Answering without words\n   2 suite: The walk and talk\n   3 suite: Busy hands\n   4 suite: The task falls apart\n   5 suite: Freeze on the line\n   6 suite: The real reaction\n   7 suite: Thinking face\n   8 suite: Stage-size acting\n   9 suite: Falling in step\n  10 suite: Bundle of nerves\n  11 pair: When a big line lands, the body freezes\n  12 pair: When the speaker gets closer to the truth, the listener leans in\n  13 pair: When the anger rises, the task gets rougher\n  14 pair: When the task falls apart, a laugh comes\n  15 pair: When they walk and talk, the shots get longer\n  16 pair: When the wind-up is big, the body stretches far on the release\nCV-CC 3: MIDI channel 3, CC 97 to 111\n   1 pair: When the eyes keep darting, the character reads as nervous\n   2 pair: When the eyes snap to something, the eyes lead the turn\n   3 pair: When a character stops blinking, they become unsettling\n   4 pair: When a touch is held, the beat turns tender\n   5 pair: When they turn their back to hide tears, the feeling stays hidden\n   6 pair: When they turn their back, the eyes stop meeting\n   7 pair: When the habit comes from lying, the gap between words and meaning grows\n   8 pair: When someone copies the habit, the two start mirroring\n   9 pair: When two people mirror each other, warmth grows between them\n  10 pair: When two people mirror each other, they stand closer\n  11 pair: When the asker pushes for words, they square off\n  12 pairs: The body tells the line\n  13 pairs: Comic business\n  14 pairs: The eyes give it away\n  15 pairs: Growing close"
   },
