   "model": "Notes",
   "data": {
    "text": "COLOR\nPatch any CV (0 to 10 V) into a jack. 0 V is the item's From setting, 10 V its To.\n\nCV-CC 1: MIDI channel 8, CC 97 to 112\n   1 Black and white to full color\n   2 Color filter\n   3 Filter color\n   4 Number of main colors\n   5 One color that pops\n   6 Warm to cool\n   7 Color change in the scene\n   8 How true skin looks\n   9 A color for each character\n  10 Color across the whole film\n  11 A color for each place or time\n  12 A color that warns\n  13 suite: Color lens\n  14 suite: The whole look\n  15 suite: Teal and orange\n  16 suite: Faded memory\nCV-CC 2: MIDI channel 9, CC 1 to 16\n   1 suite: Black and white with one color\n   2 suite: Bleak gray\n   3 suite: Color-coded worlds\n   4 suite: Red means danger\n   5 pair: When the color filter gets strong, the number of main colors drops\n   6 pair: When anger rises, the color runs warm\n   7 pair: When fear rises, the color drains\n   8 pair: When one color pops, the audience's eye locks on it\n   9 pair: When the filter turns red, the danger feels close\n  10 pair: When skin color looks far from real, the audience feels something is wrong\n  11 pair: When one person's color rubs off on a friend, the warmth grows\n  12 pair: When two people's colors fight, their egos clash\n  13 pair: When the color travels far, the hero's change shows\n  14 pair: When colors leak between worlds, the storylines cross\n  15 pair: When the warning color shows up, dread rises\n  16 pair: When one color keeps popping, it becomes a warning\nCV-CC 3: MIDI channel 9, CC 17 to 20\n   1 pairs: Color follows the feeling\n   2 pairs: One red thing\n   3 pairs: Red means run\n   4 pairs: Worlds collide"
