   "plugin": "Core",
   "model": "Notes",
   "data": {
    "text": "EMOTION\nPatch any CV (0 to 10 V) into a jack. 0 V is the item's From setting, 10 V its To.\n\nCV-CC 1: MIDI channel 10, CC 1 to 16\n   1 Strength of the feeling\n   2 How they move\n   3 Feeling in the voice\n   4 Amount of movement\n   5 Amount said\n   6 Posture changes\n   7 Size of the actions\n   8 Mood of the place\n   9 Mood of the light\n  10 Against the last scene\n  11 Feeling gap between characters\n  12 Mixed feelings\n  13 Said against meant\n  14 The eyes\n  15 The hands\n  16 Personal space\nCV-CC 2: MIDI channel 10, CC 17 to 32\n   1 Release\n   2 What the audience feels\n   3 Feeling with them\n   4 Awe\n   5 Shame\n   6 Pride\n   7 Jealousy\n   8 Relief\n   9 Too sweet\n  10 Feeling in the body\n  11 Feeling left at the end of the scene\n  12 Laughing through sadness\n  13 Tenderness\n  14 suite: Feels loving\n  15 suite: Feels joyful\n  16 suite: Feels curious\nCV-CC 3: MIDI channel 10, CC 33 to 48\n   1 suite: Feels melancholy\n   2 suite: Feels anxious\n   3 suite: Feels fearful\n   4 suite: Feels angry\n   5 suite: Feels triumphant\n   6 suite: Feels absurd\n   7 suite: Feels dreamlike\n   8 suite: Emotion lens\n   9 suite: Feeling of the scene\n  10 suite: Held-back tears\n  11 suite: Rage boils over\n  12 suite: Quiet joy\n  13 suite: Frozen fear\n  14 suite: Mood whiplash\n  15 suite: Calm in the storm\n  16 suite: The mask slips\nCV-CC 4: MIDI channel 10, CC 49 to 64\n   1 suite: Laughing through tears\n   2 suite: Brave face\n   3 suite: Dawning realization\n   4 suite: The breakdown\n   5 suite: Cold fury\n   6 suite: Giddy relief\n   7 suite: Numb shock\n   8 suite: Awkward tenderness\n   9 suite: Dread: we know, they don't\n  10 suite: Cartoon feelings\n  11 suite: Laying it on thick\n  12 suite: Struck with awe\n  13 suite: Laughing at the funeral\n  14 suite: Wanting to disappear\n  15 suite: Green with envy\n  16 suite: Proud moment\nCV-CC 5: MIDI channel 10, CC 65 to 80\n   1 suite: Right there with them\n   2 suite: A scene that lingers\n   3 suite: Gentle care\n   4 suite: Shaking with it\n   5 suite: Phew\n   6 pair: When the mood of the light drops, the strength of the feeling rises\n   7 pair: When the feeling grows stronger, the posture changes more often\n   8 pair: When a scene feels the opposite of the last one, the color shifts too\n   9 pair: When a feeling rises, the face shows it before the words\n  10 pair: When anger rises, the voice gets louder\n  11 pair: When fear rises, movement stops\n  12 pair: When one character's feeling overflows, others catch it\n  13 pair: When joy rises, the light warms\n  14 pair: When a trigger appears, the feeling turns\n  15 pair: After a release, the character is lighter\n  16 pair: When said and meant pull apart, the pauses grow\nCV-CC 6: MIDI channel 10, CC 81 to 96\n   1 pair: When people move closer, the feeling grows\n   2 pair: When tears well, the shot gets closer\n   3 pair: When we know more than they do, tension rises\n   4 pair: When feelings mix, the face flickers\n   5 pair: When someone feels loving, hearts pop onto their face\n   6 pair: When someone is joyful, a sun pops onto their face\n   7 pair: When someone turns sad, tears are drawn on\n   8 pair: When someone is anxious, they blush\n   9 pair: When someone is scared, their soul leaves their body\n  10 pair: When someone gets curious, a light bulb pops on\n  11 pair: When someone triumphs, shades pop on\n  12 pair: When things turn absurd, question marks pop on\n  13 pair: When tears are drawn on, the feeling drops\n  14 pair: When a sun pops onto a face, the feeling lifts\n  15 pair: When steam pops on, the feeling winds up\n  16 pair: When a face crackles, the feeling winds up\nCV-CC 7: MIDI channel 10, CC 97 to 112\n   1 pair: When someone laughs till they cry, the audience laughs more\n   2 pair: When the mallet bonks, the feeling turns absurd\n   3 pair: When the room feels cozy, people sit closer\n   4 pair: When the voice breaks, the tears come\n   5 pair: When the hands clench, a bigger action follows\n   6 pair: When the actions get bigger, the voice gives way\n   7 pair: When someone freezes, a slow-burn reaction follows\n   8 pair: When we see their face up close, we feel with them more\n   9 pair: When the place is huge, awe arrives\n  10 pair: When awe hits, the talking stops\n  11 pair: When awe hits, light pours in from behind\n  12 pair: When they are humiliated, shame sets in\n  13 pair: When the old wound is touched, shame comes back\n  14 pair: When shame rises, the eyes drop\n  15 pair: When shame rises, the room squirms\n  16 pair: When they make it right, relief follows\nCV-CC 8: MIDI channel 11, CC 1 to 16\n   1 pair: When pride swells, a setback follows\n   2 pair: When jealousy flares, the two drift apart\n   3 pair: When the dread lifts, relief floods in\n   4 pair: When relief comes, the breath slows\n   5 pair: When the music swells into a wall of sound, it turns too sweet\n   6 pair: When it gets too sweet, the audience pulls back\n   7 pair: When the feeling grows strong, the body shows it\n   8 pair: When their throat closes, the voice breaks\n   9 pair: When the scene fades out, the feeling lingers\n  10 pair: When the feeling lingers, the next scene feels the same\n  11 pair: When they laugh through sadness, the tears come\n  12 pair: When they laugh through sadness, the feelings blend\n  13 pair: When tenderness grows, hands are held\n  14 pair: When what they mean drifts far from what they say, sentences trail off\n  15 pairs: The body tells first\n  16 pairs: Feelings spread\nCV-CC 9: MIDI channel 11, CC 17 to 24\n   1 pairs: What isn't said\n   2 pairs: Closeness and dread\n   3 pairs: The face tells the feeling\n   4 pairs: The mood moves the feeling\n   5 pairs: Holding it in, until\n   6 pairs: Shame spiral\n   7 pairs: Too much sugar backfires\n   8 pairs: Envy turns sour"
