   "data": {
    "text": "TRANSITIONS\nPatch any CV (0 to 10 V) into a jack. 0 V is the item's From setting, 10 V its To.\n\nCV-CC 1: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 1, CC 65 to 80\n   1 Transition style\n   2 Clip animation\n   3 Fade in and out\n   4 Transition family\n   5 Intro and outro effect\n   6 Match cut\n   7 Holding before the cut\n   8 A line that jumps the cut\n   9 Cutting away before the hit\n  10 Hidden cut\n  11 Sudden black screen\n  12 suite: Classic and gentle\n  13 suite: Opening titles\n  14 suite: Time jump match cut\n  15 suite: Let it sink in\n  16 suite: Thriller cutting\nCV-CC 2: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 1, CC 81 to 96\n   1 suite: Passing the line\n   2 suite: One unbroken shot\n   3 pair: When cutting gets fast, transitions become plain cuts\n   4 pair: When the feeling turns dreamlike, shots dissolve\n   5 pair: When the pace speeds up then stops, the scene fades out\n   6 pair: When the pace races then stops, an outro effect closes it\n   7 pair: When the end loops into the start, the cut matches movement\n   8 pair: When clips bounce in, the video turns playful\n   9 pair: When transitions get explosive, something new arrives every second or two\n  10 pair: When the hold runs long, the feeling deepens\n  11 pair: When the hold goes dead silent, the silence stretches\n  12 pair: When the hold stays on a face, a cut to black follows\n  13 pair: When a line jumps the cut, the cross-cutting picks up\n  14 pair: When the answer across the cut is a gut punch, the irony bites\n  15 pair: When the film cuts away before the hit, the dread grows\n  16 pair: When the hit we missed was terrible, a slow reveal follows\nCV-CC 3: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 1, CC 97 to 102\n   1 pair: When the film cuts away to black, the black screen holds\n   2 pair: When the cuts are hidden, the tension keeps building\n   3 pair: When the screen cuts to black, time skips ahead\n   4 pair: When the black hits at the shock, everything goes silent\n   5 pairs: The hyper edit\n   6 pairs: The hit we never see"
